c(1, "header lines 1-7; §2.1 table (verbatim); §2.2 table (verbatim)", "positioning", "MyStreaks — Streak Tracker (App Store ID 1519067736; 'Improve Every Day'), formerly 'Streaking', by Streaking LLC (com.streaking.Streaker), Productivity / Lifestyle — a streak tracker with a social network around it (community feed, sharing with friends and family, Discover / Explore, comments, Groups) tied to a book and a podcast by founders Jeff & Jami; 32 reviews (every one read), 5 storefronts, 2021-02-02 → 2024-11-29, written mean 4.625 (26×5★, 4×4★, 0×3★, 0×2★, 2×1★); external (lookup API 13 Sep 2026): released 2020-09-28, version 2.75 shipped 2025-12-02, free with 10 IAP SKUs, 4 listed languages (EN, IT, JA, ZH), iOS 15.6+, also iPad / Mac / Vision; US public base 60 ratings at 4.6 (28 written = 46.7%); capabilities (verbatim): " + table("## 2.1 What MyStreaks is", 0) + " || SKUs (verbatim): " + table("## 2.2 The listed model", 0) + " — the listing advertises daily / weekly / monthly streaks, custom reminders, colour-coding and folders, photo / video / text 'Proof' posts, likes and replies to comments, an Explore feed with one-tap streak adoption, Groups, a Learn tab; the core loop in reviewers' words: 'it's a simple tap to say that you've done it, but it's so satisfying!'; '3 clicks is all it takes to update a daily streak'", "free with streak cap; Premium $5.99–$29.99; legacy Super Streaker; tip tiers $0.99–$4.99", "praise", "32 reviews; mean 4.625; US public 60 @ 4.6", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["9444357041","11900743150","9659580036"])
c(2, "How to read this table (verbatim); Seven warnings 1, 2, 4; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2; §1.3 table (verbatim); §1.4; §1.5; §1.6", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: signal bands (verbatim) " + table("## How to read this", 0) + " — 133 assignments (4.16 per review), 50 codes in 12 families, 13 unions, every code used; one review = 3.12% so the band table saturates (one review is 'Very strong', two 'High-priority') — bands reported but not trusted; every finding carries a raw count and a Wilson 95% CI; files (verbatim) " + table("## 1.1 Files used", 0) + "; coverage (verbatim) " + table("## 1.3 Coverage and reconciliation", 0) + " — GB, CA, AU and VN polled with 0 written reviews though they hold public ratings (GB 3, CA 3, AU 2, VN 1); 11 validation checks and 67 narrative checks pass; one analyst, no second rater, seven judgement calls listed; no storefront reaches 50 (US 28 = 87.5%; IT, NZ, BR, ZA one each) — no standalone country claims; negative evidence thin: 27 negative assignments, 13 negative codes on exactly one review, one review supplies 7 of 27; no version field; one non-English review (pt-BR) read in original", "n/a", "praise", "32 read; 0 eligible storefronts; one review = 3.12%", "research", "method", "generalisable", ["10372917549","9618663208"])
c(3, "Warnings 5, 6; §0.5; §7.5; §8.6 #2; part 8 #2; §8.7 #1", "data-caveat", "The corpus went silent 648 days before extraction while the app kept shipping: last written review 2024-11-29, extraction 2026-09-08; 9 of 25 public releases — including Challenges (Apr 2025), Persona Notifications (Nov 2024) and an improved Journal view (May 2025) — shipped after the last review; two readings — review flow genuinely stopped (plausible with 60 lifetime US ratings) or the collector missed 2025–26 (but _state.json marks all 9 storefronts complete and the US cursor reads 28 of 28); 'this report describes the app as it was up to late 2024… Do not read the backlog as a current bug list'; research #2 and first action: re-collect before acting on defects or builds", "shipping through Dec 2025", "none", "648 days; 9 of 25 releases unevaluated", "research", "high", "generalisable", ["12003973648"])
c(4, "Warnings 3, 7; §1.7 tables (verbatim); §0.7 sensitivity; §4.1 table (verbatim); §8.6 #3; part 8 #3", "data-caveat", "The shape of the positivity is itself a finding: 26 of 32 (81.2%) are 5★ and there is no 3★ and no 2★ review — 'a gap that a naturally-arriving review population does not usually have'; the public US histogram holds a 2★ and two more 1★ with no text — 'The silent raters are harsher than the writing ones'; two mechanisms, not separable: prompting after a success moment, or the product's shape (you are 800 days in and grateful, or stopped at the paywall in week one); integrity flags on 7 reviews (verbatim): " + table("## 1.7 Review integrity", 0) + " || " + table("## 1.7 Review integrity", 1) + " — the 38-second pair is 'the strongest solicitation signal'; one author handle is literally 'Streaking User'; a campaign-register review signs off '#streakingforthewin' urging readers to buy the book; 6 reviews (18.8%) name no product attribute; no evidence of bought reviews — consistent with in-app prompting and a founder-led community asking members to review; removing the 7 flagged leaves every headline union in its band ('The flags raise the tone of the corpus, not its structure'); distribution (verbatim): " + table("## 4.1 Distribution", 0) + " — research #3: why no 3★ or 2★", "in-app prompting; founder community", "5★-burst", "81.2% 5★; 0 3★ / 0 2★; 7 flagged; 38-second pair", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["9659580036","9659581521","6946365307","6946540196","11362194869"])
c(5, "§0.1; §3.3 N1; §4.5; §5.2 table (verbatim); §5.4 table (verbatim); §8.1 #1; §8.7 #2; §0.8 #1", "anti-pattern", "The free streak cap is the entire negative-rating story: U-MONETIZATION-ANY 3 of 32 (9.4%, CI 3.2–24.2%, mean 2.00) against 4.90 for the other 29 — the largest single split; both 1★ reviews are the cap and nothing else, and no review rated 2★ or below is about anything else; 'What is being sold is the thing the product is for' — 'i was going to make my 3rd streak and i was met with an unavoidable monthly subscription… For an app all about self betterment i thought it wouldn't require me to pay to have MORE THAN 2 GOALS' (1★); 'I was really excited about this app… But a paywall for more than 2 streaks? And it's pricey' (1★, never started); 'the worst part is that you can't have more than one streak… they could make the max like 5 or 10' (4★, pre-announcing churn — 'a more expensive signal than either 1★'); 'there are so many alternatives that don't make you pay when you've hit a max of 2 goals'; the moment of refusal (verbatim) " + table("## 5.2 What the corpus can see", 0) + " — 'it is not the price is too high… the cap is set below the point where the product does its job'; barriers (verbatim) " + table("## 5.4 Upgrade barriers", 0) + " — a 5★ user ran 3 streaks for over two years in Jan 2023, a usage shape the later free tier does not permit; §8.1 #1: re-cut the paywall to gate a feature, not the streak count", "free cap 2 → 1 streak; subscription only", "1★-burst", "3 (9.4%) mean 2.00 vs 4.90; 100% of 1★", "build-free", "moderate (n=3)", "generalisable", ["10540595375","10932357315","12003973648","9465102914"])
c(6, "§0.2 table (verbatim); §2.2 rename / referral; §5.5", "timeline", "The reported cap tightened, and the corpus is the only record of it (verbatim): " + table("## 0.2 The reported cap tightened", 0) + " — reported free allowance 3 active (Jan 2023, no cap hit) → 2 (Nov 2023, Feb 2024) → 1 (Nov 2024); in the same window the release notes show v2.58 (2024-02-28) 'Unlock unlimited streaks when 10 friends join through your invite link' — 'a referral route past the cap rather than a larger cap' — v2.62 'improved subscriptions' (2024-06-26) and v2.64 'Fix subscription bug' (2024-09-02); one reviewer reports each value, so the direction is reported, not established (the 1-cap could be a lapsed trial or a misremembered limit); every complaint post-dates November 2023; nothing published states the free cap at any date", "cap changes + referral unlock 2024", "churn", "cap 3 → 2 → 1 (reported)", "research", "limited evidence", "app-specific", ["9465102914","10540595375","10932357315","12003973648"])
c(7, "§0.3; §3.4 P2; §8.4; §0.8 #2", "positioning", "This is a social product, and that is what people praise: SOC-COMMUNITY 8 (25.0%, mean 4.88 — tied first); positive social union 11 (34.4%, CI 20.4–51.7%, mean 4.91); SOC-SHARE 3 — spouse, family, students: 'I love connecting with other Streakers on the community page. An app that encourages, uplifts, inspires'; 'The community is a wealth of knowledge & will cheer on + likely inspire more streaks'; 'it's fun to see other family member streaks and their progress (and we even have competitions sometimes too)'; 'The future of social media'; §8.4 the strategic tension — what reviewers praise most is the community, accountability and outcomes; what the company charges for is the number of streaks, 'the private, single-player counter'; what the category commoditises is that counter — 'charge for the part that is hard to copy (a real community, accountability partners, group streaks, the content ecosystem) and stop charging for the part every free competitor already gives away'; §0.8 #2: treat the community feed as the headline product", "community free / unclear; counter paid", "praise", "SOC-COMMUNITY 8 (25.0%) 4.88; social union 11 (34.4%) 4.91", "build-paid", "moderate", "generalisable", ["8444987832","9401363375","9422100038","9618210059","8393594655"])
c(8, "§0.4; §3.3 N5; §8.2 #6; §8.7 #4; §0.8 #3", "must-never-break", "The social layer's currency is forgeable: 'I feel like people cheat and just put a random number so they're on the discover feature… people still acknowledge those who have a large number of streaks' (NZ, 4★; INT-CHEAT 1) — if streak counts are editable and Discover ranks on them, 'this gets worse — not better — as the community grows'; 'the only item in the corpus whose severity is independent of how many people mentioned it'; open against 25 release notes; §8.2 #6: make streak counts non-editable, or flag edited counts on Discover — close the loophole 'before the community grows into the problem'", "editable counts rank on Discover", "complaint", "1 review; severity scales with community", "must-never-break", "low frequency, high consequence", "generalisable", ["10372917549"])
c(9, "§0.4; §3.3 table (verbatim); §3.5 table (verbatim); §8.3 table (verbatim); §8.7 #3; §0.8 #4, #5", "feature", "One review is a quarter of the defect backlog — a feedback list, not a defect rate: 10372917549 (NZ, 4★) carries 10 codes, 7 of the corpus's 27 negative assignments — reply-to-comments missing, community posting bugs, cadence not editable after creation (only retire / delete), retired streaks not viewable, editable counts inflating Discover; all eight critical reviews (verbatim) " + table("## 3.3 Prioritised negative themes", 0) + " — requests against release notes (verbatim) " + table("## 3.5 Unmet needs", 0) + " — builds with one asker each (verbatim) " + table("## 8.3 Build", 0) + " — item 10 deserves more weight: the reviewer had to retire a 6-day streak and start over to change its schedule — 'Forcing a user to destroy the exact thing the product tells them never to break is a design contradiction'; 'the cheapest item (a widget) has been open the longest, and the most consequential (the cap) has been answered with a referral mechanic rather than a product change'", "no widget; cadence fixed at creation; retired streaks hidden", "complaint", "6 requests from 3 reviewers; 5 open after 25 releases", "must-have", "low (one asker each)", "generalisable", ["10372917549","9845025034","10341126586"])
